    "body": "@HolyRoses Correct — this is dockerized Aquatic, written in Rust. Details and configuration are here: https://github.com/zootella/ftorrent/tree/master/open\n\n@1265578519 Thanks for the kernel tuning references. There are no web pages served from the announce URLs — those endpoints only speak the BitTorrent tracker protocol, so a browser request will time out as expected. The status page is at https://open.ftorrent.com/ (separate from the announce endpoints).\n\nThe architecture is being developed with Claude Code (Opus 4.6 / 4.7) and is designed to handle billions of daily requests. Based on our testing so far, we expect memory to be the bottleneck before processor or bandwidth becomes a limiting factor.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
